# Ignore rules for any build whose context is the repo root — which today means
# apps/web/Dockerfile, since the web app is an npm workspace and its lockfile
# and packages/api-types both live above it.
#
# It sits here rather than beside that Dockerfile because two builders have to
# read it: BuildKit locally and in CI, and Fly's remote builder on deploy. Only
# BuildKit understands the `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` convention; both fall
# back to `.dockerignore` at the context root.
#
# This is load-bearing, not just a size optimisation: `COPY apps/web ./apps/web`
# would otherwise drop the host's macOS-native node_modules and a stale .next on
# top of the ones the deps stage installed.
#
# The API image has its own context (apps/api) and its own apps/api/.dockerignore;
# nothing here applies to it.

**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/dist/
**/out/
**/build/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local secrets. The runtime image is configured from the environment, and the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values come in as build args.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Python: the API has its own image and none of this belongs in the web context.
apps/api/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Expo app, not part of the web build.
apps/mobile/
**/.expo/

.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
**/.DS_Store
infra/
fly.web.toml
*.md
